[2026-09-28 12:38:01] [WARNING] [Phase 1] Self-Review rejected output (Score 32). Flaws: ['The project has multiple build blockers. WeatherSkillLoader contains invalid Kotlin: `override fun definitions(): List<ToolDefinition = listOf(` is missing the closing return-type parenthesis.', 'CloudInferenceEngine has a type mismatch: ParsedChunk contains the nested CloudInferenceEngine.ToolCallFragment, while ToolCallAccumulator.add expects CloudToolCallFragment, an alias for a different top-level class.', 'ChatViewModel imports AgentOrchestrator from `com.edgehybrid.agent.domain`, but the class is in `com.edgehybrid.agent.orchestrator`. ChatScreen also lacks the lifecycle `collectAsStateWithLifecycle` and Compose `getValue` imports.', 'Hilt cannot construct the concrete parameters used by the clock and delay bindings. SystemMonotonicClock and RealSuspendDelay are objects without injectable constructors or explicit providers, so the @Binds graph is incomplete.', 'The custom `emitToFlow` and `emit` helpers invoke a FlowCollector extension from member functions without a FlowCollector receiver. They are not a valid way for those helpers to emit into the flow created by their callers.', 'Tool results are never persisted. executeTool returns a TOOL ChatMessage, but the caller only adds it to the in-memory history. The included AgentOrchestratorTest expects two persisted TOOL messages and will receive zero after the compilation problems are fixed.', 'Persisting assistant messages containing tool_calls without their matching tool results creates a dangling tool-call history. OpenAI-compatible APIs can reject the next request. This also occurs when the sixth iteration emits tool calls because the assistant tool-call message is saved before the loop stops without executing or persisting results.', 'SSE completion is detected using `receivedFrame` rather than a valid terminal event. Any clean EOF after one frame is accepted as success, even without `[DONE]` or a terminal finish reason, so a mid-sentence disconnect can be saved as a final answer. An immediate `[DONE]` also produces a successful empty completion.', 'Automatic continuation state is persisted even when recovery is abandoned. Partial assistant messages and synthetic continuation user messages remain in future history, potentially duplicating the final text or causing later turns to continue an abandoned response.', "Several conversation-store operations are outside the orchestrator's recovery handling. Failures appending system, assistant, or final messages escape the flow, skip telemetry finalization, and are reported by ChatViewModel as an unknown internal error rather than a storage recovery state.", 'The retry status is not cleared when recovered text starts streaming. After a 429/503 retry, a normal text answer can continue displaying the stale `Provider retry scheduled` status until the entire response completes.', 'The required airplane-mode UI verification is absent. There is no ChatViewModel or Compose test proving that a mid-stream network failure becomes a recovery card and retry chip without a crash; the network test only exercises the engine exception path.', 'The weather/Fahrenheit test scripts the desired sequence with fake model and tool implementations. It does not exercise CloudInferenceEngine and WeatherSkillLoader together, MCP routing, persistence, or ChatScreen, so it cannot establish the requested end-to-end one-bubble behavior.', 'No explicit IO dispatcher boundary is provided. The orchestrator and tool execution are invoked from viewModelScope, and generic SkillLoader or McpClient implementations are not forced off the caller/Main context. Ktor and Room are nonblocking today, but result parsing and future blocking tool implementations can run on the UI thread.', 'HttpMcpClient sets `initialized = true` before loadTools completes. If tool discovery fails, later calls skip initialization and reuse empty or stale bindings, while AgentToolCatalog silently converts discovery failures into an empty tool list instead of a recoverable state.', 'The cloud API key is compiled into BuildConfig and therefore recoverable from the APK. A production client should use a backend proxy or a user-specific secure authentication flow rather than embedding a provider secret.']
